Jim Foley was an experienced journalist  but his mama was worried when he went  back to Syria he'd been kidnapped once  before while working in the region still  he judged it was worth the risk  then on Thanksgiving Day in 2012 he  failed to make contact with his family  the next morning we received a call from  one of his colleagues telling us that he  had been taken you know it's just like  our worst nightmare really  Islamic extremists had her son what  followed were months of confusion and  frustration their first email was they  wanted over a 100 million euro or all  Muslim prisoners released as I feel our  government's hands were tied and not  able to negotiate if you will with the  captors at all  Dayan became increasingly desperate not  able to get answers from anyone about  what was being done to bring Jim home  that was appalling to me as an American  I just thought oh we could do better  than that's beneath us hold the while  she knew Jim was suffering they were  tortured mentally physically spiritually  in every way they could be Jim was held  nearly two years nearly starved to death  in the first year so just inhuman  conditions then an awful video appeared  on the Internet  it was Jim beheaded as he knelt in the  desert I found out when an hysterical AP  journalist called me sobbing on the  phone that's how I found out so it was  we were incredulous you know we just  weren't shocked truly really um yeah he  was 40 years old one of five siblings  the son of a mom and dad who worked  tirelessly for his release earlier today  I spoke to the Foley's and told them  that we are all heartbroken at their  loss and joined them in honoring Jim  and all that he did Jim's murder came to  symbolize his captors brutality and  hatred of the West but even though Isis  came to prominence on the president's  watch Diane doesn't blame him personally  President Obama was trying to avoid more  confrontation in Middle East but sadly  by not engaging with some of what was  happening it did worsen because there  was a void that we did not fill that  some of these jihadist groups were very  quick to fill still she has little time  for Trump's promise to bomb the hell out  of Isis instead focused on her son's  legacy and preventing other similar  tragedies there's nothing worse for a  parent than to lose a child - there  really isn't but Jim's strength and own  courage at the end of his life  challenged me as a mom in a big way that  if he could have the courage to stand up  to these folks who were doing this to  him and to do his best to protect those  he was with I too should do my best to  make things better Jim would have wanted  that Jim always wanted to make things  better for someone else
 

